Let me write the SQL query:</think>Now I'll create a query to find the three employees with the highest percentage of late orders among those with more than 50 total orders.

  → TOOL CALL: run_sql_query
    SQL: SELECT 
    e.employeeid,
    COUNT(o.orderid) AS total_orders,
    SUM(CASE WHEN o.shippeddate >= o.requireddate THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) AS late_orders,
    100.0 * SUM(CASE WHEN o.shippeddate >= o.requireddate THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) / COUNT(o.orderid) AS late_order_percentage
FROM 
    employees e
JOIN 
    orders o ON e.employeeid = o.employeeid
GROUP BY 
    e.employeeid
HAVING 
    COUNT(o.orderid) > 50
ORDER BY 
    late_order_percentage DESC
LIMIT 3

