I need to:
1. Join Musical_Preferences with Musical_Styles to get style names
2. Count how many times each style appears at each preference level (1st, 2nd, 3rd)
3. Return one row per style with counts for each preference level

Let me write the SQL query.</think>Now I'll create a query that counts how many times each musical style appears as 1st, 2nd, or 3rd preference.

  → TOOL CALL: run_sql_query
    SQL: SELECT 
    ms.StyleName AS Musical_Style,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN mp.PreferenceSeq = 1 THEN 1 END) AS First_Preference_Count,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN mp.PreferenceSeq = 2 THEN 1 END) AS Second_Preference_Count,
    COUNT(CASE WHEN mp.PreferenceSeq = 3 THEN 1 END) AS Third_Preference_Count
FROM 
    entertainmentagency.main.Musical_Preferences mp
JOIN 
    entertainmentagency.main.Musical_Styles ms ON mp.StyleID = ms.StyleID
GROUP BY 
    ms.StyleName
ORDER BY 
    Musical_Style;

